WEBVTT

00:00:14.227 --> 00:00:19.733
<i>What's this feeling I have,</i>
<i>as if I'm looking forward to...</i>

00:00:19.733 --> 00:00:25.939
<i>... somebody firing off his</i>
<i>missiles and ending everything?</i>

00:00:25.939 --> 00:00:31.378
<i>Is it a bad thing, or is this normal?</i>

00:00:31.378 --> 00:00:37.884
<i>I can't figure it out on my</i>
<i>own, so somebody tell me!</i>

00:00:37.884 --> 00:00:43.490
<i>And that person I love has once again...</i>

00:00:43.490 --> 00:00:49.930
<i>... gone far away without anybody noticing.</i>

00:00:49.930 --> 00:00:56.103
<i>Where have my dreams gone since then?</i>

00:00:56.103 --> 00:01:01.775
<i>I could swear that they</i>
<i>were right here long ago.</i>

00:01:01.775 --> 00:01:07.814
<i>We had a love that set our hearts on fire.</i>

00:01:07.814 --> 00:01:20.784
<i>Let's take back that feeling we had back then!</i>

00:02:06.339 --> 00:02:08.705
Sasami? Sasami?

00:02:14.948 --> 00:02:16.583
Yugi?

00:02:16.583 --> 00:02:20.485
Sasami, we're friends, aren't we?

00:02:22.956 --> 00:02:25.481
Sure! Of course we are!

00:02:28.929 --> 00:02:29.930
Yugi?

00:02:29.930 --> 00:02:33.422
Yugi! Yugi!

00:02:34.234 --> 00:02:35.963
Yugi!

00:02:37.037 --> 00:02:38.527
Huh?

00:02:45.078 --> 00:02:47.808
I had another dream about Yugi.

00:02:54.387 --> 00:02:56.150
What he said!

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:01.962
When one thinks of summer,
<i>tokoroten</i> soup always comes to mind.

00:03:01.962 --> 00:03:06.066
The spiciness of the mustard
always used to make my nose tingle,

00:03:06.066 --> 00:03:08.435
but this year, it seems
so pointless somehow...

00:03:08.435 --> 00:03:09.870
You want me to sing?

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:12.606
I can't talk if I'm not popular!

00:03:12.606 --> 00:03:15.575
That's the way I do things!

00:03:15.575 --> 00:03:16.910
I'm losing it!

00:03:16.910 --> 00:03:17.911
- Hm?
- I'm losing it!

00:03:17.911 --> 00:03:21.882
I lose control whenever I hold a mike!

00:03:21.882 --> 00:03:23.350
W-Washu!

00:03:23.350 --> 00:03:26.019
Hey! Long time, no see!
What's it been, half a month?

00:03:26.019 --> 00:03:28.788
What have you been doing all this time?!

00:03:28.788 --> 00:03:33.193
Terrible things have happened to
me, Ryoko's a space pirate again...

00:03:33.193 --> 00:03:36.129
No, forget about Ryoko.

00:03:36.129 --> 00:03:39.866
But Mihoshi and Kiyone are
on Pluto, and Lord Tenchi has...

00:03:39.866 --> 00:03:41.891
I have something to tell you.

00:03:42.969 --> 00:03:45.062
This is important.

00:03:48.308 --> 00:03:50.644
- Here goes!
- I got it!

00:03:50.644 --> 00:03:52.445
Grilled corn...

00:03:52.445 --> 00:03:56.074
Grilled squid... What should I eat?

00:03:57.551 --> 00:03:58.882
Hey!

00:04:03.223 --> 00:04:04.524
Here it comes!

00:04:04.524 --> 00:04:06.660
What're you lookin' at, Masaki?

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:08.389
Nothing.

00:04:09.429 --> 00:04:11.398
Sorry!

00:04:11.398 --> 00:04:14.128
C'mon, Tenchi! Come play, too!

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:18.128
Okay?

00:04:23.977 --> 00:04:26.275
Look at this.

00:04:35.589 --> 00:04:37.290
That's from...

00:04:37.290 --> 00:04:42.057
Right. These are images from when
that "Yugi" attacked the Masaki Shrine.

00:04:47.434 --> 00:04:48.868
You understand now, right?

00:04:48.868 --> 00:04:51.271
U-Understand what?

00:04:51.271 --> 00:04:56.977
I've detected Juraitrium
7000 in her bio-energy.

00:04:56.977 --> 00:05:00.714
Jurai rheumatism? What's that?

00:05:00.714 --> 00:05:02.248
Hm?

00:05:02.248 --> 00:05:04.284
Oh, my!

00:05:04.284 --> 00:05:06.119
Juraitrium 7000.

00:05:06.119 --> 00:05:09.322
Simply put, it's a bio-energy
that's unique to Juraians.

00:05:09.322 --> 00:05:13.293
Which means that Yugi
is a Juraian, just like me?

00:05:13.293 --> 00:05:14.594
That's right.

00:05:14.594 --> 00:05:19.232
I can't believe it. There's another
Juraian here on Earth besides us?

00:05:19.232 --> 00:05:20.734
Well, she's here.

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:24.471
But there aren't any
children like her on Jurai now.

00:05:24.471 --> 00:05:26.539
And how did she come to Earth?

00:05:26.539 --> 00:05:30.339
Ayeka, do you remember
those ruins in North Okutama?

00:05:32.679 --> 00:05:34.340
You don't mean...

00:05:37.183 --> 00:05:42.522
But if she's another Juraian
who's come to Earth, then...

00:05:42.522 --> 00:05:47.227
Sorry, Ayeka, but could you go
there and take a quick look around?

00:05:47.227 --> 00:05:50.594
Very well. Leave everything to me.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.869
Are you certain about this, Princess?

00:05:55.869 --> 00:05:58.004
This isn't wise.

00:05:58.004 --> 00:06:01.574
This is an emergency, so that doesn't matter!

00:06:01.574 --> 00:06:03.810
That Yugi girl is a Juraian...

00:06:03.810 --> 00:06:06.613
Princess, you don't look well.

00:06:06.613 --> 00:06:08.548
Would you like to rest a while?

00:06:08.548 --> 00:06:10.717
I'm fine. It's just that...

00:06:10.717 --> 00:06:12.185
Ma'am?

00:06:12.185 --> 00:06:15.655
How can there be another
Juraian on Earth besides us?

00:06:15.655 --> 00:06:19.292
And why did she attack the Masaki Shrine?

00:06:19.292 --> 00:06:20.760
That's a good question.

00:06:20.760 --> 00:06:22.362
We haven't the slightest idea.

00:06:22.362 --> 00:06:25.627
Yugi... Who in the world is she?

00:06:27.634 --> 00:06:29.261
O-Okay!

00:06:31.004 --> 00:06:33.006
It's cold!

00:06:33.006 --> 00:06:36.305
Yeah, this sure is the best
way to cool a watermelon!

00:06:38.211 --> 00:06:42.409
A watermelon this size
wouldn't last long at all back when...

00:06:52.692 --> 00:06:54.557
Ready to go back?

00:07:24.023 --> 00:07:26.893
Yugi!

00:07:26.893 --> 00:07:29.691
I came to play, Sasami.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:36.436
Congratulations. You two have done well.

00:07:36.436 --> 00:07:38.304
Yes, Sir! Thank you, Sir!

00:07:38.304 --> 00:07:40.039
Thank you!

00:07:40.039 --> 00:07:43.243
Due to your actions, we were
able to destroy the hideout of

00:07:43.243 --> 00:07:48.248
super-ultra class-A criminal Ryoko,
as well as round up all her henchmen.

00:07:48.248 --> 00:07:51.547
Yes, Sir! You have us to thank!

00:08:06.432 --> 00:08:09.569
Now I know what I really want.

00:08:09.569 --> 00:08:11.771
I'm not gonna listen to anybody anymore.

00:08:11.771 --> 00:08:14.107
I'm gonna do what I want
and run wild through space!

00:08:14.107 --> 00:08:18.611
You really don't care? You don't
want to go back to your life on Earth?

00:08:18.611 --> 00:08:20.747
I don't care anymore.

00:08:20.747 --> 00:08:24.184
How did we come to this?

00:08:24.184 --> 00:08:29.255
Galaxy Police HQ thinks highly of
your performance on this mission.

00:08:29.255 --> 00:08:34.260
If you manage to arrest Ryoko,
they'll have a suitable post ready for you.

00:08:34.260 --> 00:08:35.795
Really? You mean...

00:08:35.795 --> 00:08:38.765
Right. Your return to HQ is near.

00:08:38.765 --> 00:08:40.733
- Thank you, Sir!
- Thank you, Sir!

00:08:42.735 --> 00:08:47.140
I didn't really understand any
of that, but isn't it great, Kiyone?

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:48.869
Kiyone?

00:08:55.248 --> 00:08:59.118
Mihoshi and Kiyone
made a sucker out of me...

00:08:59.118 --> 00:09:00.551
But...

00:09:02.055 --> 00:09:03.852
But...

00:09:07.427 --> 00:09:10.055
I haven't had that much fun in a long time.

00:09:11.164 --> 00:09:13.766
What is it? You look happy.

00:09:13.766 --> 00:09:15.668
Yeah, a little.

00:09:15.668 --> 00:09:18.933
It's been a while, so maybe
I'll go back to Earth for a bit...

00:09:20.106 --> 00:09:23.376
I suppose you're right.
That might be a good idea.

00:09:23.376 --> 00:09:26.346
There's someone on Earth
that you want to see, right?

00:09:26.346 --> 00:09:28.371
Somebody I want to see?

00:09:29.949 --> 00:09:32.051
Who would wanna go to Earth?

00:09:32.051 --> 00:09:34.520
I'm Ryoko the space pirate!

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:36.956
Why would I possibly wanna go
to a backwoods dump like Earth?

00:09:36.956 --> 00:09:39.322
Really? I suppose you're right.

00:09:48.968 --> 00:09:52.805
Come on in, Yugi! The cold water feels great!

00:09:52.805 --> 00:09:56.409
Oh. Okay.

00:09:56.409 --> 00:09:57.243
It's cold!

00:09:57.243 --> 00:09:58.778
Are you okay?

00:09:58.778 --> 00:10:01.542
Yeah. It feels good, though.

00:10:04.317 --> 00:10:07.387
I just had a dream about you, Yugi,

00:10:07.387 --> 00:10:11.391
so when you really
showed up, I was surprised!

00:10:11.391 --> 00:10:12.881
Really?

00:10:14.427 --> 00:10:17.630
This is beautiful.
It's green everywhere you look.

00:10:17.630 --> 00:10:21.534
Yeah! I like the scenery here, too.

00:10:21.534 --> 00:10:23.303
'Cause it looks like Jurai.

00:10:23.303 --> 00:10:25.038
Jurai?

00:10:25.038 --> 00:10:29.075
I wish I could live forever in a
place like this. With you, Sasami.

00:10:29.075 --> 00:10:30.109
Huh?

00:10:30.109 --> 00:10:33.613
We're friends, right? Friends forever.

00:10:33.613 --> 00:10:35.103
Huh?

00:10:37.016 --> 00:10:39.280
Yugi?

00:11:03.142 --> 00:11:07.580
This is terrible. The energy to the
Jurai Tree has been completely cut off.

00:11:07.580 --> 00:11:10.116
That must be what broke the seal.

00:11:10.116 --> 00:11:14.487
Azaka, can you retrieve anything
from it, even if only the memory?

00:11:14.487 --> 00:11:17.523
If we were to supply it
with energy, I believe so.

00:11:17.523 --> 00:11:18.458
Do it.

00:11:18.458 --> 00:11:20.085
- Yes, Ma'am!
- Yes, Ma'am!

00:11:28.901 --> 00:11:31.461
Now retrieving data.

00:11:42.181 --> 00:11:44.484
Data retrieval complete.

00:11:44.484 --> 00:11:49.288
Will now project.

00:11:49.288 --> 00:11:53.493
One score and seven years into
the reign of Queen Hinase of Jurai,

00:11:53.493 --> 00:11:56.062
an evil mutant possessed of terrible power,

00:11:56.062 --> 00:11:58.931
though but six years of age, did awaken.

00:11:58.931 --> 00:12:01.267
The 27th year of Hinase's reign?

00:12:01.267 --> 00:12:03.703
Princess, in that year,
there was a cataclysm

00:12:03.703 --> 00:12:07.473
that brought Jurai to
the brink of destruction.

00:12:07.473 --> 00:12:12.240
Does that mean that the mutant
behind it was sealed in here?

00:12:29.862 --> 00:12:31.664
Yugi!

00:12:31.664 --> 00:12:34.565
They're all your friends, Yugi!

00:12:36.436 --> 00:12:38.301
My friends...

00:12:48.314 --> 00:12:51.517
I was alone... always alone.

00:12:51.517 --> 00:12:54.577
I was lonely, so I created some friends.

00:12:59.492 --> 00:13:02.154
Come on, everyone! Let's play!

00:13:18.077 --> 00:13:24.050
With her powers, the mutant
plunged Jurai into chaos.

00:13:24.050 --> 00:13:28.885
Nothing could combat her terrible power.

00:13:49.675 --> 00:13:51.438
Stop!

00:13:54.614 --> 00:13:56.048
Stop! Don't!

00:13:56.048 --> 00:13:58.073
Please, stop!

00:13:59.952 --> 00:14:04.290
Queen Hinase did rise up
and use her own arcane powers

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:07.560
to subdue the mutant.

00:14:07.560 --> 00:14:11.087
Stop! Stop it! What have I done wrong?

00:14:30.349 --> 00:14:33.886
Ye spirits just of heart, grant me power

00:14:33.886 --> 00:14:37.219
and bestow eternal
slumber upon this evil one!

00:14:54.907 --> 00:14:57.176
Stop! Stop it!

00:14:57.176 --> 00:14:59.245
I hate the dark!

00:14:59.245 --> 00:15:04.182
I hate... I hate being alone!

00:15:15.328 --> 00:15:18.297
Child, you have done no wrong.

00:15:18.297 --> 00:15:21.801
However, your power is too dangerous.

00:15:21.801 --> 00:15:27.406
I'm sorry, but there is nothing else I can do.

00:15:27.406 --> 00:15:29.242
Forgive me.

00:15:29.242 --> 00:15:34.347
With her arcane powers,
Queen Hinase did seal up the mutant,

00:15:34.347 --> 00:15:38.384
and so that she would never
again awaken, did banish her

00:15:38.384 --> 00:15:45.157
deep into space to the frontier,
where planets are most sparse.

00:15:45.157 --> 00:15:48.361
To the frontier, where
planets are most sparse...

00:15:48.361 --> 00:15:51.931
By some fluke, it landed here on Earth.

00:15:51.931 --> 00:15:54.200
What a trick of fate!

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:59.138
Who could imagine that 3,500 years later

00:15:59.138 --> 00:16:02.471
we would visit Earth,
where the Seal Temple fell?

00:16:17.323 --> 00:16:18.924
What's wrong, Yugi?

00:16:18.924 --> 00:16:23.418
Did something sad happen
to you? You look lonely.

00:16:25.531 --> 00:16:29.902
Maybe... Maybe you
shouldn't create friends...

00:16:29.902 --> 00:16:32.871
Everyone picks on me!

00:16:36.776 --> 00:16:41.270
Don't worry! Nobody here
would ever pick on you, Yugi!

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:46.183
Sure...

00:16:49.355 --> 00:16:55.061
I see. So Yugi is the Juraian
mutant who was sealed in those ruins.

00:16:55.061 --> 00:16:57.196
So, now we know who our enemy is.

00:16:57.196 --> 00:17:00.599
But why do you suppose
she attacked the Masaki Shrine?

00:17:00.599 --> 00:17:03.502
For revenge, because we're Juraians?

00:17:03.502 --> 00:17:05.438
That's probably not all.

00:17:05.438 --> 00:17:09.075
It's just that Yugi's reawakening
and the breakup of the Tenchi Family

00:17:09.075 --> 00:17:11.477
are pretty tightly synced.

00:17:11.477 --> 00:17:13.079
Right.

00:17:13.079 --> 00:17:16.105
It's too unnatural to be a coincidence.

00:17:21.087 --> 00:17:23.789
I wanna go on this place's thrill rides!

00:17:23.789 --> 00:17:26.158
Uh... I have a problem with those.

00:17:26.158 --> 00:17:28.861
You're such a scaredy-cat, Tenchi!

00:17:28.861 --> 00:17:31.931
How about here, then?

00:17:31.931 --> 00:17:34.525
A parasite museum?

00:17:38.704 --> 00:17:40.039
What was that?

00:17:40.039 --> 00:17:41.939
I'll go look.

00:17:48.948 --> 00:17:50.282
Washu?!

00:17:50.282 --> 00:17:55.921
Oops. I knew the coordinates
would be off if I attached it in a hurry.

00:17:55.921 --> 00:17:59.258
Why is there a lady from Okayama
popping out of your toilet, Tenchi?

00:17:59.258 --> 00:18:04.563
Sorry, Tenchi, but could you
come back to Okayama for a bit?

00:18:04.563 --> 00:18:07.333
It looks like something is going on.

00:18:07.333 --> 00:18:11.070
I heard all about that from Ayeka.
She said everyone split up.

00:18:11.070 --> 00:18:13.272
Suddenly and simultaneously.

00:18:13.272 --> 00:18:14.907
Tenchi, doesn't it bother you?

00:18:14.907 --> 00:18:19.276
Sure it does, but maybe it's just coincidence.

00:18:19.578 --> 00:18:22.481
Then did you know that the
Masaki Shrine was attacked?

00:18:22.481 --> 00:18:24.817
Huh? The shrine? Who by?!

00:18:24.817 --> 00:18:27.286
Well, that would take a while to explain...

00:18:27.286 --> 00:18:28.821
Then how are Grandpa and the others?

00:18:28.821 --> 00:18:30.222
They're okay. Barely.

00:18:30.222 --> 00:18:32.758
Looks like the attacker wasn't going all-out.

00:18:32.758 --> 00:18:34.627
Really? Thank goodness...

00:18:34.627 --> 00:18:39.732
But something is definitely
starting to happen. Something big.

00:18:39.732 --> 00:18:41.066
Will you come back?

00:18:41.066 --> 00:18:42.301
A-All right.

00:18:42.301 --> 00:18:44.069
You can't!

00:18:44.069 --> 00:18:47.106
Didn't you say that we'd have
fun this summer, just the two of us?!

00:18:47.106 --> 00:18:49.508
Didn't you say that you'd
stay with me the whole summer?!

00:18:49.508 --> 00:18:51.076
Sakuya...

00:18:51.076 --> 00:18:53.840
I'm sorry, Washu. I'll get ready.

00:18:57.049 --> 00:18:57.883
Sakuya...

00:18:57.883 --> 00:19:01.954
Why? Why are you going back?!
Stay with me, Tenchi!

00:19:01.954 --> 00:19:03.556
I'm sorry, Sakuya, but...

00:19:03.556 --> 00:19:06.192
The people in Okayama are
more important to you than I am?!

00:19:06.192 --> 00:19:09.855
No, of course not. That's not it...

00:19:11.297 --> 00:19:13.933
This is bad! My grandpa's
been in an accident!

00:19:13.933 --> 00:19:16.469
Mr. Tsuchida? How is he?

00:19:16.469 --> 00:19:19.905
He's okay. He was riding his scooter
alone when he fell and hurt his back.

00:19:19.905 --> 00:19:22.942
The thing is, he has a traffic safety
purification ceremony in a minute!

00:19:22.942 --> 00:19:25.377
Masaki, you've gotta do it for him!

00:19:25.377 --> 00:19:27.913
What?! I can't do anything like that!

00:19:27.913 --> 00:19:30.916
That's okay! Just do some
poses that look like you're doing it!

00:19:30.916 --> 00:19:33.352
It'd be too embarrassing to
say that the shrine's head priest

00:19:33.352 --> 00:19:36.255
had an accident and couldn't do
the traffic safety purification, right?

00:19:36.255 --> 00:19:37.256
L-I guess...

00:19:37.256 --> 00:19:40.960
Sorry, Washu. I can't go back right now.

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:42.495
It can't be helped, I guess.

00:19:42.495 --> 00:19:43.863
Come on, hurry up!

00:19:43.863 --> 00:19:45.698
Hold on, I'm coming!

00:19:45.698 --> 00:19:46.732
My, my...

00:19:46.732 --> 00:19:51.103
I guess it won't change anything if
Tenchi comes back to Okayama now.

00:19:51.103 --> 00:19:54.940
It'll be a while before I'm done
analyzing this thing, anyway.

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:57.773
I guess I'll head back.

00:20:05.618 --> 00:20:07.086
It's sure gotten quiet...

00:20:07.086 --> 00:20:11.590
Yeah, it's evening already.
Everybody's gone home.

00:20:11.590 --> 00:20:12.658
Sasami.

00:20:12.658 --> 00:20:13.592
Huh?

00:20:13.592 --> 00:20:17.596
Come to my place. Let's live there together.

00:20:17.596 --> 00:20:24.126
The others will be gone soon,
so come live with me. Forever.

00:20:28.707 --> 00:20:32.006
You're my friend, right, Sasami?

00:20:33.512 --> 00:20:35.681
What're you saying, Yugi?

00:20:35.681 --> 00:20:40.209
We're still kids. We can't live by ourselves.

00:20:42.755 --> 00:20:44.780
Fine! See if I care!

00:20:54.333 --> 00:20:56.062
Yugi!

00:21:00.506 --> 00:21:02.337
Yugi...

00:21:35.608 --> 00:21:39.211
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:39.211 --> 00:21:43.115
<i>Sleeping late, staying up late,</i>
<i>and napping all the time!</i>

00:21:43.115 --> 00:21:46.719
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:46.719 --> 00:21:50.656
<i>Sneaking bites to eat, midnight</i>
<i>snacks, and pouring tea on my rice!</i>

00:21:50.656 --> 00:21:54.159
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>
<i>I just can't stop it, I just can't stop it...</i>

00:21:54.159 --> 00:21:58.130
